# Targets chezmoi deletes on apply.
#
# XDG autostart leftovers from the KDE setup. uwsm runs XDG autostart entries
# too, so with these in place Discord and Steam each launch twice -- once from
# here and once from hypr/autostart.lua, which is where they are now defined
# (with their workspace placement).
#
# Listed here rather than deleted once because both applications rewrite the
# file whenever their in-app "launch on startup" option is toggled. If they
# keep coming back, turn that setting off inside Discord and Steam as well --
# this only cleans up after them.
.config/autostart/discord.desktop
.config/autostart/steam.desktop

# The two fcitx5 overrides, deleted from this repo but not from the machines
# that already applied them. Removing a file from the source tree does NOT
# remove the copy in $HOME -- chezmoi just stops managing it -- so both would
# sit there as orphans, still carrying --disable=notificationitem and still
# naming /usr/bin/fcitx5. Verified rather than assumed: source file deleted,
# re-applied, target still present.
#
# On Arch that is merely stale, and quietly misleading: the path is right, so
# the tray icon stays suppressed by the old file and the waybar ignore-list
# that replaced it never actually gets exercised. You would think it worked.
#
# Anywhere else the D-Bus one is broken rather than stale -- it overrides the
# packaged service with a binary that is not there, so the first app to ask
# for org.fcitx.Fcitx5 activates nothing and the input method is simply gone.
# See "Tray" in the README.
.local/share/dbus-1/services/org.fcitx.Fcitx5.service
.config/autostart/org.fcitx.Fcitx5.desktop
